[UTCDate "2021.01.20"]
[UTCTime "13:25:51"]

1. b4 { White gives up centre space. Opens a line for the bishop. And the reason for the two squares is to kick away the black knight on b8 if it comes. } 1... e5 { Black takes the opportunity to grab some space in the centre and at the same time attacking the pawn on b4. } { [%cal Ge7b4] } (1... a5 2. b5 Nf6) (1... d5 2. Bb2 Nf6 { [%cal Rb2f6,Rf8b4] } (2... Qd6 { This move allows black to capture the center by attacking the pawn on b4 and defending e5 } { [%cal Gd6b4,Gd6d5,Gd6e5] } 3. b5 { This is mistake because the black Queen can fork the pawn and the bishop } (3. a3 e5 { So whit the Queen black has captured the whole center } 4. Nf3 { Put pressure on the center } 4... f6 { Shutting down the diagonal of the white bishop. } { [%cal Rb2h8] } 5. e3 { Adding to the pressure on the center } { [%cal Gc2c4] } 5... Be6 6. d4 { Black has the center space but white has spave on the Queen side } { [%cal Ge5e4,Gf3d2,Gc2c4] }) 3... Qb4) 3. e3 Bf5 4. a3 (4. Nf3 e6 5. c4 Bxb4 (5... c6 6. b5) 6. Qa4+ Nc6 7. Nd4 (7. Ne5) 7... Rb8 8. Nxc6 (8. Nxf5 exf5 9. a3 Ba5 10. Be2 O-O 11. cxd5) 8... bxc6 9. Qxc6+) 4... e6) 2. Bb2 { Black can offer the b4 pawn in exchange for the e5 pawn. } { [%cal Gf8b4,Gb2e5] } 2... Bxb4 (2... f6 { This shuts down the diagonal for the bishop on b2. The open diagonal tot the king is no threat because the white Queen is enclosed. } { [%cal Gh5e8,Rd1h5,Rb2g7] }) (2... Nc6 { Not wise, because the white pawn can attack the knight } 3. b5 Nd4 4. e3 Ne6 5. Bxe5 { White wins pawn }) 3. Bxe5 { This looks like a good position for white with both central pawns still alive, but black can attack the bishop and develop at the same time and has more open lines to develop. } 3... Nf6 { Prevent the bishop from taking g7 and develop. } 4. Nf3 Nc6 { White wants to preserve the bishop } 5. Bb2 d5 { Open the line for the bishop and taking the centre. } 6. e3 { Open a path for the bishop and Queen. } 6... O-O 7. Be2 { Finsh developement } (7. c4 { Attack the centre. After exchange white could use it's two pawns dominating the centre. }) *


